{title: Buried in Shamir}
{subtitle: Judges 10:1–2; 10:2}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Tola son of Puah stood up [Bb]
A [Cm]man of Issachar by blood [Gm]
He rose to deliver Israel [Bb]
From the [F]weight of the [Gm]flood
He lived in Shamir the hill [Bb]
In the [Cm]country of Ephraim still [Gm]
A place where the shadows lie [Bb]
And the [F]quiet winds blow by [Gm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He judged Is[Bb]rael twen-ty-three [F]years
And then [Gm]he died and [Bb]was buried [F]there
In [Gm]Shamir the hill [Bb]country of Ephraim [F]
[Eb]Resting in the earth so deep and [Gm]dim
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He maintained the law and order [Bb]
In [Cm]times of peace and [Gm]calm
No great wars to fight or fear [Bb]
Just the [F]daily toil and work
The [Gm]minor judge among them all
Keeping the people true [Bb]
In the [Cm]hill country of Ephraim
Where the roots run deep and blue
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]He judged Is[Bb]rael twen-ty-three [F]years
And then [Gm]he died and [Bb]was buried [F]there
In [Gm]Shamir the hill [Bb]country of Ephraim [F]
[Eb]Resting in the earth so deep and [Gm]dim
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]After Abimelech [Gm]he rose
[Eb]To stand in the justice [Gm]line
[Eb]Tola son of Puah known
In [Gm]the heart of Issachar's vine
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He judged Is[Bb]rael twen-ty-three [F]years
And then he [Gm]died and [Bb]was buried [F]there
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
